= Utility (decision theory) — Technical =

An ordinal utility u represents preference ≼ when <pre>A ≼ B ⇔ u(A) ≤ u(B)</pre>. For von Neumann–Morgenstern expected utility over lotteries, admissible utility functions are unique up to positive affine transformations <pre>u'(x)=a u(x)+b, a&gt;0</pre> when the representation axioms hold.

== Modeling cautions ==
* utility ≠ money
* utility ≠ happiness by definition
* utility representation ≠ proof that preferences are rational or ethically justified

